{"variant": "compliance", "year": 1989, "month": 7, "day": 27, "slug": "workforce-reduction-notice-6654", "variant_int": 1, "html": "<section class=\"page-banner\"><div class=\"container\"><p class=\"text-uppercase mb-1\" style=\"color:var(--gold);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.18em;font-size:.75rem\"><a href=\"/archive/\" style=\"color:var(--gold)\">Archive</a> &rsaquo; <a href=\"/archive/1989/\" style=\"color:var(--gold)\">1989</a> &rsaquo; <a href=\"/archive/1989/07/\" style=\"color:var(--gold)\">07</a> &rsaquo; 27</p><p style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,.6);font-size:.72rem;margin-bottom:.4rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase\">Compliance Review &bull; KDR-1989-Q3-6283</p><h1 style=\"font-size:clamp(1.2rem,3vw,2rem);line-height:1.25\">Independent Review — Workforce Reduction Notice</h1><p style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,.7);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:0\">eSports &amp; Competitive Gaming &bull; Windermere Partners &bull; Archived 1989-07-27</p></div></section><section style=\"padding:3rem 0;background:var(--surface)\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"row g-4\"><div class=\"col-lg-8\"><div id=\"acpwb-compliance-7b031b24-header\" style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:4px solid var(--gold);padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;margin-bottom:2rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:.5rem\">Document Information</div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.3rem .8rem;font-size:.83rem;margin-bottom:.75rem\"><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Client</span><br><strong>Windermere Partners</strong></div><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Industry</span><br><strong>eSports &amp; Competitive Gaming</strong></div><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Audit Ref</span><br><code style=\"font-size:.75rem\">KDR-1989-Q3-6283</code></div><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Version</span><br><code style=\"font-size:.75rem\">1.1</code></div></div><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\">Filed by <strong>Deepak Delaney</strong>, Director, Academic Workforce Analytics &mdash; <a href=\"mailto:deepak.delaney@acpwb.com\" style=\"color:var(--navy)\">deepak.delaney@acpwb.com</a></div><div style=\"margin-top:.6rem;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.3rem\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;padding:.15rem .45rem;background:#f4f6f9;border:1px solid #dde1e8;color:#444\">NASDAQ Listing Rule 5600 Series (board and committee requirements)</span><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;padding:.15rem .45rem;background:#f4f6f9;border:1px solid #dde1e8;color:#444\">IRC §4960 (excise tax on excess tax-exempt organization executive compensation)</span></div></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">1. Engagement Scope</h5><p style=\"font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333\">This document constitutes the final report for the 1989 annual HR compliance audit for Windermere Partners. The scope encompassed a review of 63 policies and procedures, a sample of 10 personnel files, and interviews with 12 HR and payroll staff members.</p></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">2. Methodology</h5><p style=\"font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333\">The methodology for this review was based on the &quot;Three Lines of Defense&quot; model, assessing the roles and effectiveness of business operations (first line), compliance and risk functions (second line), and internal audit (third line) in managing NASDAQ Listing Rule 5600 Series (board and committee requirements); IRC §4960 (excise tax on excess tax-exempt organization executive compensation) risk.</p></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">3. Findings Summary</h5><div style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><table class=\"dash-table w-100\"><thead><tr><th>Finding ID</th><th>Risk</th><th>Status</th><th>Owner</th><th>Due</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">KDR-3870-001</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;border:1px solid #fcd34d\">MEDIUM</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#dcfce7;color:#15803d;border:1px solid #86efac\">REMEDIATED</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Director of Internal Investigations</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">1989-10-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">Union information requests for bargaining unit data were not fulfilled within the required timeframe</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">KDR-3674-002</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569;border:1px solid #cbd5e1\">INFO</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;border:1px solid #fcd34d\">IN PROGRESS</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Manager of Corporate Communications</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">1989-09-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">Summary Plan Descriptions (SPDs) for 63 benefit plans have not been updated to reflect recent plan amendments</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">KDR-8378-003</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef9c3;color:#854d0e;border:1px solid #fde047\">LOW</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#eff6ff;color:#1d4ed8;border:1px solid #93c5fd\">MONITORING</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Director of Government Relations</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">1989-09-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">Automated employment decision tool bias audit not conducted as required by NYC Local Law 144</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">KDR-5108-004</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;border:1px solid #fcd34d\">MEDIUM</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#eff6ff;color:#1d4ed8;border:1px solid #93c5fd\">MONITORING</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Vice President of Brand</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">1989-09-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">Salary range disclosure missing from 17% of job postings in jurisdictions requiring it</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">KDR-3094-005</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569;border:1px solid #cbd5e1\">INFO</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;border:1px solid #fcd34d\">IN PROGRESS</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Vice President of Government Affairs</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">1989-10-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">Summary Plan Descriptions (SPDs) for 63 benefit plans have not been updated to reflect recent plan amendments</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">4. Detailed Findings</h5><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">KDR-3870-001</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;border:1px solid #fcd34d\">MEDIUM</span><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#dcfce7;color:#15803d;border:1px solid #86efac\">REMEDIATED</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Union information requests for bargaining unit data were not fulfilled within the required timeframe</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Revise the employee handbook to remove language that could be interpreted as restricting employees&#x27; Section 7 rights under the NLRA. Submit revised handbook to labor counsel for review within 60 days.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">This issue has been escalated to the executive steering committee for prioritization and resource allocation. A formal response will be provided following the committee&#x27;s next scheduled meeting on 1989-07-27.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Director of Internal Investigations</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>1989-10-28</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">KDR-3674-002</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569;border:1px solid #cbd5e1\">INFORMATIONAL</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Summary Plan Descriptions (SPDs) for 63 benefit plans have not been updated to reflect recent plan amendments</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Automate the COBRA notification process to ensure qualifying event notices are generated and mailed within 5 business days of the triggering event.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">The finding is valid. A budget of $63K has been approved to procure the necessary technology to automate this control. Implementation is projected to take 10 weeks.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Manager of Corporate Communications</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>1989-09-28</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">KDR-8378-003</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef9c3;color:#854d0e;border:1px solid #fde047\">LOW</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Automated employment decision tool bias audit not conducted as required by NYC Local Law 144</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The COBRA administration vendor&#x27;s performance will be audited quarterly to ensure compliance with all statutory notification deadlines, with financial penalties for non-compliance.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">This finding relates to a legacy system that is scheduled for decommissioning on 1989-07-27. Given the impending system retirement, management has accepted the risk for the interim period and will not invest in remediation for the legacy system.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Director of Government Relations</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>1989-09-28</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">KDR-5108-004</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;border:1px solid #fcd34d\">MEDIUM</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Salary range disclosure missing from 17% of job postings in jurisdictions requiring it</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The HRIS will be audited and reconfigured to ensure FMLA leave entitlement calculations are 100% compliant with the &quot;rolling 12-month period measured backward&quot; method.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">The finding is acknowledged. This issue was caused by a temporary system outage on 1989-07-27. The system has been restored, and the backlog of affected transactions has been cleared. We consider this matter closed.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Vice President of Brand</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>1989-09-28</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">KDR-3094-005</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569;border:1px solid #cbd5e1\">INFORMATIONAL</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Summary Plan Descriptions (SPDs) for 63 benefit plans have not been updated to reflect recent plan amendments</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Review and revise all pre-employment and post-offer medical questionnaires to remove any questions related to family medical history or genetic information.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">This finding relates to a legacy system that is scheduled for decommissioning on 1989-07-27. Given the impending system retirement, management has accepted the risk for the interim period and will not invest in remediation for the legacy system.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Vice President of Government Affairs</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>1989-10-28</strong></div></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-top:1.5rem;padding-top:1.25rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border);display:flex;justify-content:space-between\"><a href=\"/archive/1989/07/26/construction-and-contech-strategy-5990/\" style=\"font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none\">&larr; Previous</a><a href=\"/archive/1989/07/27/workforce-reduction-notice-6654/erisa-compliance-review-9627/\" style=\"font-size:.85rem;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none\">Next &rarr;</a></div></div><div class=\"col-lg-4 d-none d-lg-block\"><div style=\"position:sticky;top:2rem\"><div class=\"acpwb-card mb-3\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:.7rem\">Audit Record</div><dl class=\"mb-0\" style=\"font-size:.82rem\"><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Audit Ref</dt><dd class=\"mb-2\" style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.75rem;opacity:.7\">KDR-1989-Q3-6283</dd><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Date</dt><dd class=\"fw-700 mb-2\">1989-07-27</dd><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Organization</dt><dd class=\"fw-700 mb-2\">Windermere Partners</dd><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Findings</dt><dd class=\"mb-2\">5 total</dd><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Record ID</dt><dd class=\"mb-0\" style=\"font